      "alt": "I seem to have empirically eliminated DoS bugs from my web server as a category by instructing ChatGPT to write a profiler to find every single location in the code along the request path that a DoS could even theoretically occur because it's a resource that an attacker could control, and then test it under load with the deployment benchmark tests so it simulates real web apps, and then go through all of the resulting 3000 locations by hand and put them into categories/clusters, then further categorize them as potential DoSes or not, then make a giant formal resource ledger based on the profiling results of every single data structure in the request path and prove that these cannot be pushed into a state that DoSes the server, during which I watched it go through and find the remaining DoS flaws after the ledger flagged their potential to exist and patch them all.",
